# ModP / P Language Patterns

- Project file: `modp/KnirvNetwork.pproj` — must register every new `.p` source file
- Events: always import from `modp/events/network_events.p` before using in component machines
- Component machines go in `modp/components/<layer>/` matching the network layer
- Network invariants: `modp/monitors/network_invariants.p` — add monitors for new protocol properties
- Composition tests: `modp/tests/network_composition_tests.p`
- Run via testnet: `cd packages/KNIRVTESTNET && make test-modp`
- Run directly: `bash modp/scripts/run-tests.sh`
- Results land in `modp/results/` and `modp/PCheckerOutput/BugFinding*/`
- Requires `dotnet` runtime for PChecker; falls back to syntax-validation mode without it
- Every new async protocol interaction (IBC transfer, oracle governance, DVE validation) needs a P machine
- Integration test hook: `integration-tests/modp_formal_verification_test.go`
- KNIRVTESTNET formal verification config: `packages/KNIRVTESTNET/.env` (MODP_DIR setting)
